+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Give each task a unique id
+
+The app needs a stable reference to a task that survives a rename.
+
+- `add` returns a task with an `id`: a string no other task of the list has (never reused, even after `remove`).
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning `Result<Task>` like the other methods.
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+  When a string is both an id and another task's title, the id wins.
+- Ids come from a per-list counter (the domain may not use clock or randomness).
